{"id": "EUVD-2026-101061", "enisaUuid": "0e0f23ce-b17e-3bce-95c8-9ea75a6d5691", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\npower: sequencing: fix NULL-pointer dereference in pwrseq_unit_new()\n\nIf memory allocation fails in pwrseq_unit_setup_deps(), pwrseq_unit_put()\nis called to release the partially initialized unit. However, we've\nnever initialized unit->list and pwrseq_unit_release() will\nunconditionally call list_del() on it. Initialize unit->list right after\nallocating the unit struct.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T13:27:44", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:19:06", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/29e03670cc384561a2037c69b0a1cc5232d3c6c3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/859880b07a75c7a29d141abfacbd750d25a8e920", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6e571aea60de7f4c62b77510495d1bcc7df406a1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/115b303e8e093d964089ec6f3c40d984d77b33d0"], "aliases": ["GHSA-hmfx-pr93-vm36", "CVE-2026-98412"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0a031404-e1e0-3b54-8807-cfc353257f9d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "249ebf3f65f8530beb2cbfb91bff1d83ba88d23c <6e571aea60de7f4c62b77510495d1bcc7df406a1"}, {"id": "2f6b4b6a-c395-3d9e-9d1a-c4f8f6021423", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "249ebf3f65f8530beb2cbfb91bff1d83ba88d23c <859880b07a75c7a29d141abfacbd750d25a8e920"}, {"id": "59ebf54c-24e2-3a0e-83ef-1750ead71b49", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "6694095e-eced-335e-8475-13dd5218b9e1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "81ede525-3d57-33f1-ae90-f9933be628a0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "249ebf3f65f8530beb2cbfb91bff1d83ba88d23c <29e03670cc384561a2037c69b0a1cc5232d3c6c3"}, {"id": "b